-- | A loop label, with its trailing space — or nothing.
-- |
-- | `'outer loop` puts the label **before** the keyword, which is Rust's
-- | placement and `examples/control.sdx`'s. A `break` puts it after, so that
-- | form is written at its own call site rather than here: one helper that
-- | knew both positions would be a helper whose callers had to know which it
-- | was doing.
-- |
-- | The stored label excludes the quote, as the token's does.
export(crate) label_text : &Option<String> -> String
label_text label = case label of
  Some name -> format! \-> "'#{name} "
  None -> String::new ()
